  "id": "COMPOUND:15051 - PROTEIN:83",
  "verbalization": "Ludongnin G appears to interact with the Glucagon receptor through multiple indirect pathways, with the receptor being a target of several compounds that are themselves targets of the drug. The evidence suggests that Ludongnin G may act as a modulator of the Glucagon receptor via a series of biochemical intermediates, including Werner syndrome ATP-dependent helicase, Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 9, and Protoxylocarpin E. These intermediates are all targets of compounds that have been identified as having a relationship with the Glucagon receptor. The integration of these pathways implies that Ludongnin G may influence the Glucagon receptor through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially affecting signaling pathways that regulate glucose metabolism and cellular response to hormonal signals. The presence of multiple distinct targets, each linked to the Glucagon receptor through different molecular mechanisms, suggests a multifaceted interaction that may involve diverse cellular processes.",
